            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0242" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.3393/622: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Myers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-07T23:00:00+08:00">September 7,
                            1939—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 13—1:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. This afternoon my Japanese colleague called and after stating that Japan
                    will remain strictly neutral in the European war and that it will concentrate on
                    the China affair informed me that he had this morning asked the British Acting
                    Consul General and [the French?] Consul General to withdraw their gunboats from
                    Canton waters. He added that this information was being conveyed to me and the
                    Italian Consul under instructions from his Government.</p>
                <p>It is understood that the Consuls concerned have referred the matter to their
                    respective Governments. It may be mentioned that the French gunboat is now in
                    Hong Kong and that Japanese agreement to its return to Canton might be difficult
                    to obtain. There is one British gunboat here.</p>
                <p>It will be recalled that shortly after the commencement of the World War the
                    German gunboat at Canton was disarmed and placed in the custody of the customs
                    and that the British and French gunboats were withdrawn from Canton waters.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
